## §6.1.2–6.1.3: *Telezentrik*, *Televarianz* vs. *Dysvarianz* & $\Dext$ {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-d">STRATUM D: TELEZENTREN, EXTINKTIONSDISKRIMINANTE &amp; DIMENSION FOLIATIONS (SM, PP. 108–118)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="48%"}
### *Telezentrik* Without Retrocausality
* Evolutionary curves in an *äonische Area* are channeled by asymptotic attractor submanifolds of maximal coherence and minimal entropy—**Telezentren ($T_z$)**.
* Anticipates **Karl Friston's Free-Energy Principle (2010)** and **Andy Clark's Active Inference (2016)**: self-organizing systems persist by following forward local gradients ($-\grad\Psi$) toward viable attracting sets.

::: {.firewall-box .fragment}
***Televarianz* vs. *Dysvarianz* & The *Extinktionsdiskriminante* ($\Dext$):**
* **Televarianten ($\mathbf{W}_{\mathrm{tele}} \subset \mathcal{B}(T_z)$):** Preserve internal *telezentrische Tektonik* while dissipating entropy toward $T_z$.
* **Dysvarianten ($\mathbf{W}_{\mathrm{dys}}$):** Cross the phase-space boundary—the **Extinktionsdiskriminante ($\Dext = \partial\mathcal{B}(T_z)$)**:
  - *Functional Dysvarianz (Prop. 6.9):* Rule architecture intact, but syndrome populations become undefined (initial/intermittent).
  - *Structural Dysvarianz:* Internal Kombinat fractures across $\Dext$ (final extinction $\to \nullsyntrix$).
:::

:::

::: {.column width="52%"}

