## §6.2.1: Phase Manifolds $\MAR$ & Far-Centered Collectors (Fig. 6.1) {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-a">STRATUM A: METRIC DYNAMICAL SYSTEMS &amp; HETEROCLINIC COLLECTORS (DEFS. 6.1–6.5)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="48%"}

::: {.thm-box}
**Definitions 6.1, 6.2 & 6.5: Area Phase Manifold & Basins of Attraction**
An *äonische Area* is a complete Riemannian manifold $(\MAR, \gAR)$ equipped with a complete smooth vector field $\XAR \in \mathfrak{X}(\MAR)$ generating the flow $\Phi_t \colon \MAR \to \MAR$.
A compact invariant submanifold $\mathcal{A} \subset \MAR$ ($\Phi_t(\mathcal{A}) = \mathcal{A}$) is a **Telecentric Attractor** with open basin:
$$
\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{A}) \;\coloneqq\; \left\{ x \in \MAR \;\middle|\; \lim_{t \to \infty} \dist_{\gAR}\big(\Phi_t(x), \mathcal{A}\big) = 0 \right\}
$$
(Open panoramas without affine telecentres adjoin ideal boundary points at infinity as **projective telecentres**, Def. 6.5).
:::

::: {.carnap-box .fragment}
**Definition 6.4: Far-Centered Collector Bifurcation Cycle (*Kollektor* $\mathfrak{Col}$)**
1. **Polydromy Point ($x_0 \in \Dext$):** Critical saddle where $d\XAR(x_0)$ has $P_\mu > 1$ unstable directions ($W^u(x_0) \cong \mathbb{R}^{P_\mu}$).
2. **Far-Centered Collector ($\mathcal{K}$ at distance $L > 0$):** Asymptotic attractor whose basin captures the punctured unstable tuft $W^u_{\mathrm{tele}}(x_0) \coloneqq W^u(x_0) \setminus \{x_0\} \subseteq \mathcal{B}(\mathcal{K})$:
$$
\lim_{t \to \infty} \dist_{\gAR}\!\Big( \Phi_t\big(W^u_{\mathrm{tele}}(x_0)\big),\; \mathcal{K} \Big) = 0
$$
:::

:::

::: {.column width="52%"}

<div class="interactive-panel">
  <h4>Interactive Far-Centered Collector Bifurcation Cycle (Fig. 6.1)</h4>
  <p class="widget-context-note">
    <b>Context (Def. 6.4):</b> Adjust unstable tuft dimension $P_\mu > 1$ and flow parameter $s \in [0, 1]$ to trace how trajectories branching from Polydromy saddle $x_0 \in \Dext = \partial\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{K})$ reconverge into the Far-Centered Collector $\mathcal{K}$ at distance $L > 0$.
  </p>
  <div class="slider-row">
    <span style="color:#FFA500;">Unstable Dim <i>P<sub>μ</sub></i>:</span>
    <input type="range" id="col-pmu" min="2" max="6" step="1" value="4" oninput="updateCollectorLab()">
    <span id="col-pmu-val" style="font-family:monospace; width:22px;">4</span>
