  <div id="col-readout" class="matrix-readout" style="margin-top:6px; font-size:0.64em;"></div>
</div>

<div class="video-container" style="margin-top:8px;">
  <video autoplay data-autoplay loop muted playsinline src="media/Ch6_Act4_Collector_Bifurcation.mp4" style="max-height:185px;"></video>
  <div class="video-caption">Manim Act IV (Fig. 6.1): Polydromic Branching Tuft W^u(x₀) Reconverging into Collector 𝔎</div>
</div>

:::

::::

::: {.notes}
When a trajectory reaches an unstable saddle x_0 (a Polydromiepunkt), its unstable manifold W^u(x_0) branches into a tuft of P_mu directions. Definition 6.4 formalizes Heim's Kollektor as a far-centered asymptotic attractor K whose basin B(K) captures the entire punctured unstable manifold W^u_tele(x_0), reconverging the branching paths.
:::

