## §6.2.2: Final Telecentric Coalgebra $(\nu\mathcal{T}, \zeta)$ & Stage V Phase-Lock {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-a">STRATUM A: UNIVERSAL COALGEBRA (THM. 6.7), LAMBEK LEMMA (PROP. 6.8) &amp; STAGE V</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="48%"}

::: {.interactive-panel}
#### Interactive 4-Tab Inspector: Universal Coalgebra & Lambek Isomorphism

<p class="widget-context-note">
  <b>Context (§6.2.2, Def. 6.6, Thm. 6.7, Prop. 6.8 &amp; Carnap 6.1):</b> Click each tab to inspect how Universal Coalgebra formalizes *Telezentrik* as the unique mediating homomorphism $!_\alpha \colon S \to \nu\mathcal{T}$ without retrocausal forces.
</p>
<div class="syn-tabs">
  <button class="syn-tab-btn active" onclick="showCoalgTab(1, this)">1. Path Signature T_ℝ</button>
  <button class="syn-tab-btn" onclick="showCoalgTab(2, this)">2. Final Coalgebra νT</button>
  <button class="syn-tab-btn" onclick="showCoalgTab(3, this)">3. Lambek Proof (Prop 6.8)</button>
  <button class="syn-tab-btn" onclick="showCoalgTab(4, this)">4. Carnap 6.1 Explication</button>
</div>

::: {#coalg-pane-1 .syn-tab-pane .active}
**1. Basepoint-Preserving Telecentric Path Signature $\mathcal{T}_{\mathbb{R}}$ (Def. 6.6)**
In the locally presentable category of diffeological spaces $\mathbf{Diff}_{\mathrm{smooth}}$ (Souriau 1980; Iglesias-Zemmour 2013), fix time-horizon step $\epsilon > 0$:
$$
\mathcal{T}_{\mathbb{R}}(M) \;\coloneqq\; \Big( M \times C^\infty\big([0, \epsilon], M\big) \Big)_{\operatorname{ev}_0 = \operatorname{pr}_1} \;\amalg\; \mathbf{1}
$$
where $\gamma(0) = x$ enforces basepoint continuity and $\mathbf{1} = \{\ast_{\mathrm{term}}\}$ represents terminal exhaustion ($\nullsyntrix$).
:::

::: {#coalg-pane-2 .syn-tab-pane}
**2. Existence of Final Telecentric Coalgebra $(\nu\mathcal{T}, \zeta)$ (Thm. 6.7, Fig. 6.2)**
For every candidate dynamical system $(S, \alpha \colon S \to \mathcal{T}(S))$, there exists a **unique telecentric coalgebra homomorphism** $!_\alpha \colon S \to \nu\mathcal{T}$:
$$
\begin{matrix}
S & \xrightarrow{\;\;\alpha\;\;} & \mathcal{T}(S) \\
\downarrow\scriptstyle\exists!\,!_\alpha & \circlearrowright & \downarrow\scriptstyle\mathcal{T}(!_\alpha) \\
\nu\mathcal{T} & \xrightarrow[\;\;\sim\;\;]{\;\;\zeta\;\;} & \mathcal{T}(\nu\mathcal{T})
\end{matrix}
$$
:::

::: {#coalg-pane-3 .syn-tab-pane}
**3. Constructive Banach Contraction & Lambek Isomorphism (Prop. 6.8)**
Along the terminal sequence $\mathbf{1} \leftarrow \mathcal{T}\mathbf{1} \leftarrow \mathcal{T}^2\mathbf{1} \leftarrow \cdots \leftarrow \nu\mathcal{T} = \lim_k \mathcal{T}^k\mathbf{1}$:
* Regarding $(\mathcal{T}\nu\mathcal{T}, \mathcal{T}\zeta)$ as a coalgebra supplies $\eta \colon \mathcal{T}\nu\mathcal{T} \to \nu\mathcal{T}$ with $\zeta\eta = \mathcal{T}(\eta\zeta)$.
* Since $\zeta$ is a coalgebra morphism, $\eta\zeta = \operatorname{id}_{\nu\mathcal{T}}$ by finality, whence $\zeta\eta = \mathcal{T}(\operatorname{id}) = \operatorname{id}_{\mathcal{T}\nu\mathcal{T}}$!
:::

::: {#coalg-pane-4 .syn-tab-pane}
**4. Carnap 6.1: Eliminating Retrocausal Metaphysics**
* Algebras over a monad ($T_{\mathsf{P}}(X) \to X$) fold parts inward (bottom-up construction); coalgebras ($S \to \mathcal{T}(S)$) unfold state transitions outward in time (Rutten 2000; Jacobs 2016).
* The unique map $!_\alpha \colon S \to \nu\mathcal{T}$ classifies present states by their forward asymptotic equivalence class without violating local efficient causality!
:::

:::

