</div>

::: {.thm-box .fragment}
**Theorem 6.21(1): Variational Free-Energy $W_2$-Gradient Flow**
Under Langevin noise $dx_t = -\grad\Psi\,dt + \sqrt{2\varepsilon_{\mathrm{fluct}}}\,dW_t$, the Fokker–Planck density $\rho_t \in \mathcal{P}_2^{\mathrm{ac}}(\MAR)$ is the steepest-descent $2$-Wasserstein gradient flow of **Variational Free Energy**:
$$
\Ffree[\rho] \coloneqq \int_{\MAR}\Psi\rho\,d\operatorname{vol}_g + \varepsilon_{\mathrm{fluct}}\int_{\MAR}\rho\ln\rho\,d\operatorname{vol}_g, \quad \frac{d}{dt}\Ffree[\rho_t] = -\int \|\grad(\Psi+\varepsilon\ln\rho_t)\|^2\rho_t \le 0
$$
:::

:::

