::::

::: {.notes}
Section 6.3.4 elevates two of Heim's deepest dynamical claims into theorems of differential topology and stochastic analysis. Theorem 6.20 proves via the Poincare-Hopf and Morse Index Theorems on an Euler-zero isolating region that the number of secondary critical centers mu = c_0 + c_1 = 2c_0 is strictly even. Theorem 6.21 proves that metastable states near D_ext obey the Wasserstein free-energy gradient flow and Eyring-Kramers escape law, triggering Resynkolation when the barrier drops below the safety threshold.
:::

