## §6.4–6.6: Reconstruction Map $\mathcal{R}$, Sanity Checks & Synthesis {.smaller}

<div class="stratum-badge badge-c">STRATUM C: EXPLICATION 6.1, COMPLETION OF TEIL A &amp; PIVOT TO CHAPTER 7 (TEIL B)</div>

:::: {.columns}

::: {.column width="54%"}

| Heimian Concept ($\mathbf{D}$) | Mathematical Explicatum ($\mathcal{R}$ in $\mathbf{A}/\mathbf{B}$) | Status & Ref. |
|:---|:---|:---:|
| **Äonische Area ($\mathfrak{AR}$, Eq. 27)** | Riemannian phase manifold $(\MAR, \gAR, \Phi_t)$ | **A-Def** (Def. 6.1) |
| **Telezentrik** | Final coalgebra terminality & Lyapunov gradient flow | **A-Def** (Def. 6.6) |
| **Telezentrum ($T_z$)** | Final coalgebra $(\nu\mathcal{T}, \zeta)$ & attractor $\mathcal{A} \subset \MAR$ | **A-Thm** (Thm. 6.7) |
| **Kollektor ($\mathfrak{Col}$)** | Far-centered attractor capturing tuft $W^u_{\mathrm{tele}}(x_0) \subseteq \mathcal{B}(\mathcal{K})$ | **A-Def** (Def. 6.4) |
| **Televariante ($\mathbf{W}_{\mathrm{tele}}$)** | Basin trajectory with exponential decay $\dot{V} \le -\gamma V$ | **B-Thm** (Thm. 6.10) |
| **Extinktionsdiskriminante** | Morse–Smale Whitney separatrix $\Dext = \partial\mathcal{B}(\mathcal{A})$ | **B-Thm** (Thm. 6.14) |
| **Telezentralenrelativität** | Left-adjoint non-preservation $\Gamma_m(\nu\mathcal{T}_m) \not\cong \nu\mathcal{T}_{m+1}$ | **B-Thm** (Thm. 6.19) |
| **Even Secondary Parity ($\mu$)** | Morse–Poincaré–Hopf index identity $\mu = 2c_0 \equiv 0 \pmod 2$ | **B-Thm** (Thm. 6.20) |
| **Resynkolation** | Kramers escape recovery switching $(\mathcal{O}_{\mathrm{syn}}, \Psi) \mapsto (\mathcal{O}'_{\mathrm{syn}}, \Psi')$ | **B-Thm** (Thm. 6.21) |

::: {.thm-box .fragment}
**Physical & Epistemic Sanity Checks (§6.5):**
1. **Unpolarized Flat Limit ($\grad\Psi \equiv 0$):** $\XAR = 0 \implies \Phi_t = \operatorname{id}$; no finite telecenters exist ($\mathcal{A} = \emptyset$), recovering Heim's *pseudotelezentrisch* projective panorama (SM, p. 108).
2. **Adjoint Non-Preservation:** $\Gamma_m \dashv U_{m+1}$ proves mathematically that terminal goals cannot remain absolute across transcendence levels.
:::

:::

::: {.column width="46%"}

::: {.carnap-box}
**Carnapian Explication 6.1: *Telezentrik* as Terminal Coalgebraic Invariant**
Replaces retrocausal metaphysics with Lambek's isomorphism $\zeta \colon \nu\mathcal{T} \xrightarrow{\sim} \mathcal{T}(\nu\mathcal{T})$, the unique universal morphism $!_\alpha \colon S \to \nu\mathcal{T}$, and Polyak–Łojasiewicz free-energy dissipation $\dot{V} \le -\gamma V$.
:::

<div class="video-container">
  <video autoplay data-autoplay loop muted playsinline src="media/Ch6_Act12_Synthesis.mp4" style="max-height:210px;"></video>
  <div class="video-caption">Manim Act XII (Fig. 6.5): Synthesis of Telecentric Coalgebras, Separatrices &amp; Stratum Relativity</div>
</div>

::: {.firewall-box .fragment}
**Completion of *Teil A* & Dialectical Bridge to Chapter 7 (*Teil B*):**
By proving that telecentric attractors act as terminal coalgebras and that purpose is mathematically relative across transcendence levels, the universal categorical logic of **Teil A** is complete. To interface this abstract machinery with empirical science and physical measurement, **Chapter 7 (*Anthropomorphic Syntrometry*)** executes the **Anthropomorphic Pivot**: restricting the observer site to algebraic number fields $\mathbf{Coeff} = [\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{R} \subseteq \mathbb{C}]$ and continuous parameter spaces $R_n$.
:::

:::

::::

::: {.notes}
We conclude Chapter 6—and with it the entire first part (Teil A) of Syntrometrische Maximentelezentrik. In Chapter 7, we cross into Teil B: executing the Anthropomorphic Pivot to the number fields Q, R, C and continuous parameter spaces R_n.
:::

